# Source Adapter Rules

Every external vacancy source MUST implement the common SourceAdapter abstraction.

Never expose source-specific response formats outside the adapter.

Before writing a scraper investigate in this order:

1. official API
2. RSS or feeds
3. public structured JSON
4. static HTML
5. browser automation

Browser automation is a last resort.

---

Every adapter must support:

fetch_new_items()

health_check()

rate limiting

timeouts

retry with backoff

logging

incremental collection

---

Do not fetch the complete source history on every execution.

Maintain source cursors such as:

last_item_id

last_timestamp

pagination cursor

---

Every received item must keep provenance:

source_id

source_item_id

source_url

source_created_at

first_seen_at

raw_payload

---

Do not perform scoring inside SourceAdapter.

Adapter responsibilities end after retrieving and normalizing the source item.

Pipeline responsibilities must remain separate.